<item><title>Planning your next software project</title><dc:creator><![CDATA[nexora]]></dc:creator><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A useful starting point is a clear problem statement. Describe the people who will use your product, the tasks it should support, and what a successful outcome looks like.</p><h2>Start with the essentials</h2><p>Prioritize a small set of valuable features. Agree on milestones and feedback sessions before implementation begins.</p>]]></content:encoded><excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded><wp:post_id>7</wp:post_id><wp:post_date>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date><wp:post_date_gmt>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date_gmt><wp:comment_status>closed</wp:comment_status><wp:ping_status>closed</wp:ping_status><wp:post_name>planning-software</wp:post_name><wp:status>publish</wp:status><wp:post_parent>0</wp:post_parent><wp:menu_order>7</wp:menu_order><wp:post_type>post</wp:post_type><wp:is_sticky>0</wp:is_sticky></item>
<item><title>A practical approach to cloud migration</title><dc:creator><![CDATA[nexora]]></dc:creator><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Before moving workloads, inventory your applications, dependencies, and data. Understand availability requirements and the costs of your current infrastructure.</p><h2>Plan for continuity</h2><p>Test migrations with noncritical workloads first. Document rollback steps and validate backups before any production transition.</p>]]></content:encoded><excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded><wp:post_id>8</wp:post_id><wp:post_date>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date><wp:post_date_gmt>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date_gmt><wp:comment_status>closed</wp:comment_status><wp:ping_status>closed</wp:ping_status><wp:post_name>cloud-migration</wp:post_name><wp:status>publish</wp:status><wp:post_parent>0</wp:post_parent><wp:menu_order>8</wp:menu_order><wp:post_type>post</wp:post_type><wp:is_sticky>0</wp:is_sticky></item>
<item><title>Security starts with everyday habits</title><dc:creator><![CDATA[nexora]]></dc:creator><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Strong security combines practical controls with habits people can maintain. Keep software updated, use multifactor authentication, and review access regularly.</p><h2>Make recovery part of the plan</h2><p>Test backups and define who responds when an incident occurs. Review your procedures as your organization changes.</p>]]></content:encoded><excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded><wp:post_id>9</wp:post_id><wp:post_date>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date><wp:post_date_gmt>2026-01-01 12:00:00</wp:post_date_gmt><wp:comment_status>closed</wp:comment_status><wp:ping_status>closed</wp:ping_status><wp:post_name>security-habits</wp:post_name><wp:status>publish</wp:status><wp:post_parent>0</wp:post_parent><wp:menu_order>9</wp:menu_order><wp:post_type>post</wp:post_type><wp:is_sticky>0</wp:is_sticky></item>
